    "body": "@dbaron, but isn't nesting divs or tables in `p` or heading elements invalid in HTML? For `p`, the HTML parser simply prevents this by auto-closing the `p` just before the next non-phrasing element, so it's possible only in XML mode (as in your example) or as a result of the direct DOM manipulation. Should the spec describe the behavior of the invalid markup in the section on the regular rendering?",
